# Read by GitHub's "Cite this repository" button, and by Zenodo.
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use rostree in your work, please cite the version you used.
title: "rostree: explore and analyse ROS 2 package dependency graphs"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Erwin
    family-names: Lejeune
repository-code: "https://github.com/guilyx/rostree"
url: "https://guilyx.github.io/rostree"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
abstract: >-
  rostree resolves the dependency graph of ROS 2 packages from package.xml
  manifests and answers questions about it: what a package depends on, why it
  depends on another, what depends on it, and what changed since a snapshot. It
  treats the graph as a directed acyclic graph rather than a tree, so every
  analysis is linear in the size of the workspace. It ships as a Python library,
  a command-line tool, a terminal UI and a self-contained interactive HTML graph.
keywords:
  - ROS 2
  - robotics
  - dependency analysis
  - software engineering
  - graph algorithms
  - visualization
